Fresh Peach Cobbler
  --Lindsay, Pinch of Yum

Filling:
5–6 large fresh yellow peaches, sliced (~5 c, or 750-900 g)
1/4 c sugar
1 tbsp cornstarch (optional)

Preheat the oven to 350F. Smear the bottom of 9×13" pan with a little bit of butter. Add peaches and sugar, and mix directly in the pan.

Topping:
1/2 c salted butter, melted
3/4 c sugar
1 tsp vanilla
1 c flour
1 tsp baking powder
a pinch of salt
1/4 c turbinado sugar (optional, but really nice)
whipped cream or vanilla ice cream for serving

Mix the butter, sugar, vanilla, flour, baking powder, and salt until a cookie-dough-like batter forms. Place scoops of the mixture over the top of the peaches. Spread with a spoon or with your fingers – no need for perfection here. Bake for 30 min. At this point it should be juicy and bubbly around the sides. Sprinkle the top with turbinado sugar. Bake another 10-15 min and then finish with a few min under the broiler (475F-ish) for a few minutes to get it golden brown and slightly crunchy on top. (Just keep a close eye on it because it can burn quickly.) To get a thick saucy peach base, let it stand for 20-30 min before serving with some vanilla ice cream.


Notes: If it looks too soupy after mixing peaches with sugar, add the cornstarch. If it looks dry after baking 25 min, pour 2 tbsp melted butter over peaches. Works with fresh and frozen (thaw first), not canned. No need to peel.
